==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 60~66.67 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[M. Ost]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*2 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*5 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*5 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is generally considered the hardest in the sub-chapter. You have barely any time to scrape up some cash before you are hit with waves of Condemned Pengs and an M. Ost. The best strategy is to use [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-immune units]], which can keep their ground during the Condemned Pengs' [[Death Surge]]s. If you have [[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Cat's]] True Form, he is very useful as he can dodge all three threats in the stage. [[Rich Cat III (Super Rare Cat)|Richest Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] with the Extra Money [[Talents|Talent]] can help a lot with money. [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]], if one has him, completely trivializes this stage by targetting both major enemies in this stage.

